<rml>
<head>
	<title>Remember Password Prompt</title>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="base.rcss"/>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="remember_password_prompt.rcss"/>
</head>
<body>
	<!-- Modern theme's own copy of the "remember password" OK/Cancel confirmation. Per-theme file
	     (UI::RmlBridge::LoadThemedDocument) because modern-frame/modern-frame-accent (plus the
	     -crimson palette variant) is genuinely modern-specific structure, not just style -- the
	     shared ../../remember_password_prompt.rml is legacy's own theme-neutral copy and carries
	     neither class (architecture-principles.md §15: a "shared" file must not bake in one
	     theme's vocabulary). Keep this file's ids/data-model/event-callback names in sync with
	     ../../remember_password_prompt.rml -- RememberPasswordPrompt.cpp binds against both by the
	     same names. -->
	<div id="panel" class="modern-frame modern-frame-crimson center-both" data-model="remember_password_prompt">
		<div class="modern-frame-accent modern-frame-accent-crimson frame-accent"></div>
		<span class="prompt-title">{{title_text}}</span>
		<span class="prompt-body">{{body_text}}</span>
		<div class="btn btn-ok" data-event-click="prompt_ok_click">{{ok_label}}</div>
		<div class="btn btn-cancel" data-event-click="prompt_cancel_click">{{cancel_label}}</div>
	</div>
</body>
</rml>
